The paves of an edge whose pave blocks do not chain: no write past the
array's end (mitcad#1559).

BOPDS_DS::Paves collects the distinct paves of an edge's pave blocks into
an array of the blocks' number plus one, as a chain of n blocks has n + 1
paves, and only asserts that (in debug builds). Blocks that do not chain
(two ending at one vertex at parameters that differ, as on edges of a
pipe shell's corner where BRepFill_TrimShellCorner intersects its two
sides) have more distinct paves, and the loop wrote past the array's end:
the heap was corrupted ("corrupted size vs. prev_size", an IFC file's
closed stirrup of lines and arcs swept as a pipe, valgrind: an invalid
write of 8 bytes just after a block of 64 in BOPDS_DS::Paves called from
MakeFacesSec and FindFromVEdge). The array now holds every distinct pave,
counted first.

